--- !u!114 &1819902984
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1819902983}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b0f7ef1062ea19e49b238f82235db37e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::IntroController
  textComponent: {fileID: 64047385}
  skipTextUI: {fileID: 1666478338}
  introPanel: {fileID: 1615188800}
  fadeScreen: {fileID: 1817412579}
  fadeSpeed: 2
  introParts:
  - "1997.                  \n\nCity of Derry Police Department and Hurricane, Utah
    Police Department had both reported something unusual in their missing persons
    cases."
  - "Bill Denbrough, 13, disappeared without a trace.                                      
    \n\nCassidy Andrews, 8, also went missing under similar circumstances.\n\nAt
    first, the cases were treated as unrelated incidents\u2026 different states,
    different lives, no clear connection.\n\nBut then the reports started to overlap.\nStrange
    sightings.\nUnmarked locations.\nPeople refusing to talk about what they saw."
  - "The official investigations were quietly closed.\n\nThat\u2019s when I got involved."
  - "I\u2019m a detective / field investigator, brought in unofficially to look into
    what the police couldn\u2019t\u2014or wouldn\u2019t\u2014explain. My assignment
    was simple on paper:\n\nFind the truth behind the disappearances.\n\nNo witnesses.
    No clear suspects. No bodies.\n\nOnly fragments.\n\nTen notes were recovered
    across the region\u2014hidden, scattered, almost as if someone wanted them to
    be found, but not easily."
  - "Each note contains pieces of what actually happened here. Not just evidence\u2026
    but something closer to a confession.\n\nSomething wrong is tied to this place.\n\nAnd
    the deeper I go, the clearer it becomes:\n\nThis was never just a missing persons
    case.\n\nIt was something else entirely.\n\nSo I came here, to the last known
    location connected to both cases.\n\nTo search.\n\nTo piece together the truth.\n\nTo
    find out what really happened to Bill Denbrough and Cassidy Andrews\u2026\n\n\u2026and
    why I might not be the first investigator to try."
  typingSpeed: 0.05
